<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9500" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">compactĭlis</span></b> , e, adj.
		compactus, compingo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pressed</i> or <i>joined
			together</i>, <i>compact</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trabes,</span>”
				<i>fitted one to another</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 4,
					7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">postes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 14, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">operimentum (of nuts),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 22, 24, § 88</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Of
			form, <i>thick-set</i>, <i>compact;</i>
			of lions, <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 16, 18, § 46</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">of bees,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					11, 18, 19, § 59</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
